Setting up .Data Directories & Starting S-Plus:

% mkdir .Data
% Splus

# S-PLUS : Copyright (c) 1988, 1998 MathSoft, Inc.
# S : Copyright Lucent Technologies, Inc.
# Version 5.0 Release 3 for Sun SPARC, SunOS 5.5 : 1998 
# Working data will be in .Data 
 
!!! Warning: Different hardware platforms need different .Data directories !!!

If Splus finds a .Data directory, it will use this directory to store all
its data and user written functions. If NO .Data directory exists,
Splus will create a new data directory called Schapterxxxx, where xxxx
represents the process number of the Unix Splus process.
Note that every Schapterxxxx directory contains a .Data subdirectory.

% Splus

# Creating data directory for chapter
# S chapter initialized.
# S-PLUS : Copyright (c) 1988, 1998 MathSoft, Inc.
# S : Copyright Lucent Technologies, Inc.
# Version 5.0 Release 3 for Sun SPARC, SunOS 5.5 : 1998 
# Working data will be in /home/symanzik/Schapter793 


Exiting S-Plus:

> q()


If you want to use a previously created data directory Schapterxxxx
in another Splus session (that creates another data directory
Schapteryyyy), this can be done using the attach command:

> attach("Schapter793")

Note that new data and user written functions will be written to
the new Schapteryyyy/.Data directory. The old one will not be modified.

Alternatively, you can cd into the Schapterxxxx directory and
start Splus from there. Since in this case a local .Data directory
is available, Splus will use this directory. No new Schapteryyyy
directory will be created.

