Solution to the famous birthday problem: Assuming birthdays
are uniformly distributed over the year, how many people do
I have to select randomly to obtain a probability >= 0.5
that at least 2 people have the same birthday, i.e.,
P(at least 2 identical birthdays) = 1 - P(no identical birthday)

n _ 1
pno _ 1
while (pno > 0.5) 
{
